      "observation": "The player camera (Image 2) suffers from severe visual distortion and low resolution, making the scene appear pixelated and lacking detail. The bridge and keep geometry are visibly aliased and poorly defined compared to the high-resolution detail views (Images 3 and 4).",
      "correction": "Increase the player camera's render resolution to match the detail camera's 257 native terrain resolution. In Unity, this can be achieved by setting the camera's 'Render Texture Resolution' to a high value (e.g., 2048x2048) and ensuring the 'Quality Settings' are set to 'High' or 'Ultra' for the target platform."
    },
    {
      "observation": "The lighting in the player camera (Image 2) is inconsistent with the detail camera (Image 3). The detail camera shows warm, directional lighting with clear highlights and shadows, while the player camera appears flat and lacks depth, making the scene look unconvincing.",
      "correction": "Reconfigure the player camera's lighting to match the detail camera. In Unity, adjust the 'Directional Light' component to match the angle and intensity of the detail camera's light. Add a 'Lighting' > 'Baked Lightmap' or 'Realtime Lighting' setup to ensure consistent illumination across all views."
    },
    {
      "observation": "The material separation between the keep, bridge, and terrain is poor in the player camera (Image 2). The textures appear blended and lack clear boundaries, reducing the scene's visual clarity and realism.",
      "correction": "Apply distinct, high-resolution materials to each object in the player camera. In Unity, use the 'Material' component to assign unique materials to the keep, bridge, and terrain. Ensure that the materials have proper 'Shader' settings (e.g., 'Standard' or 'Unlit') and 'Texture' settings (e.g., 'Normal Map' and 'Specular') to enhance visual separation."
    }
  ],
  "reference_similarity_estimate_0_to_10": 6.5,
  "uncertainty": "The player camera's visual quality is significantly degraded compared to the detail camera, making a precise similarity estimate challenging. The distortion and low resolution introduce uncertainty in the assessment of architectural details and material separation."
